        "number": 10,
        "internalPageId": 10,
        "title": "Language Targets",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "Language Targets",
          "Descriptive Functions Examples 1 Give an opinion -This is a beautiful city. - It is not. It is crowded and noisy. 2 State size They have a big house. 3 Describe shape We need a round table. 4 State age We live in an old building. 5 Define color The sky is blue today! 6 Determine origin It is a German dog. 7 State material Please, buy some plastic cups. 8 State purpose He has a sports car.",
          "Adjectives can be used in any tense: present, past, future. They are mainly used to describe different characteristics. Check the following examples.",
          "TO CONSIDER More than one adjective can be used to describe one single thing. It has to respect the order presented in the characteristics. E.G. They have a gorgeous, big, new, American, wooden, beach house. *not always all the characteristics are used*"
        ],
